{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":103560,"duration_api_ms":102817,"num_turns":9,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"cef8d3a3-0916-410f-88dd-6963f4797611","total_cost_usd":0.4763345499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31689,"cache_read_input_tokens":225370,"output_tokens":2787,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31689,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":8,"outputTokens":2787,"cacheReadInputTokens":225370,"cacheCreationInputTokens":31689,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.38045625000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":46,"outputTokens":3094,"cacheReadInputTokens":236223,"cacheCreationInputTokens":45392,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.09587830000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"The amendment identifies a real, verified bug in the save-load path. `reconcile_stability_tracker` conflates \"field is present in JSON\" with \"tracker baselines are valid,\" which fails for legacy schema-2 saves that serialized `StabilityTracker::default()` sentinel values before seeding was introduced. The code, default values, and update logic all confirm the described false instability spike. The proposed fix (detect and reseed the legacy-default case) is safe and backward-compatible, and a regression test is warranted since no existing tests cover this path.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-6-e15be02d","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified in code: `reconcile_stability_tracker` (save.rs:350-361) only reseeds when the stability_tracker field is absent. A legacy schema-2 save that serialized `StabilityTracker::default()` (sentinels: 25.0°C, 7.0 pH, 7.0 GH_d, 8.0 DO mg/L) will pass the `has_serialized_stability_tracker` check, so stale baselines survive loading untouched. `update_stability_tracker` (shrimp.rs:93-121) then computes swings against these sentinel values — with the pH divisor of 0.5 and a 0.3 rise factor, even a modest real-water pH difference triggers an instability_index jump to ~0.3, exactly as described. Detecting the legacy-default sentinel pattern and reseeding is the correct fix: even in the unlikely event a legitimate tracker exactly matches the defaults, reseeding to current water state is harmless. A regression test for a v2 payload with a present-but-uninitialized tracker is necessary since current tests only cover the missing-field branch."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"8d100af5-75fb-418f-812a-bc305a5bfeda"}
